---
name: Jane Doe
summary: One or two sentences for the index and the featured card.
location: Asheville, NC
medium: Linocut and screenprint

# Where this artist sits in the rotation. Lower goes first.
#
# The feature changes every Wednesday at 9am Eastern and works down this list,
# starting again at the top when it reaches the end. Give a new artist the next
# number after the highest already in use, and they will come up in turn.
featureOrder: 2

# Required. A profile without this is never shown — not in the list, not
# featured, not in the sitemap.
#
# It stays in the file rather than being assumed because it is the one fact
# about an artist that is not on their website: whether they said yes. Set it
# to false while a page is being drafted or checked, and the whole profile
# stays invisible until somebody deliberately changes it.
permission: true

# Order here is the order shown. Put the shop first.
links:
  - label: Shop
    href: https://example.com/shop
  - label: Instagram
    href: https://instagram.com/example
  - label: Website
    href: https://example.com

# Optional. Use an image the artist has given you, and credit it.
# image: /images/artists/jane-doe.webp
# imageCredit: "Mothman print, 2025. Courtesy of the artist."
---

A few paragraphs about the work. What they make, how they make it, what drew
them to this material.

Write about the work rather than around it. "She has been carving lino blocks
of Appalachian folklore since 2019, mostly at night, and the linework has got
progressively wilder" says more than a paragraph of adjectives.

Keep it short. The point of the page is the links at the bottom.
